sentences.t:
Ter circum accensos cincti fulgentibus armis
decurrere rogos, ter maestum funeris ignem
lustravere in equis ululatusque ore dedere;

sentences.l:
Three times around the lit, girt with gleaming arms,
they ran, the pyres, three times the grieving, of the funeral, fire
they circled on horses, and wailings from their mouths gave;

sentences.t:
Hic alii spolia occisis derepta Latinis
coniciunt igni, galeas ensesque decoros
frenaque ferventisque rotas;

sentences.l:
Here others spoils, from the slain, stripped, Latins
throw on the fire, helmets and swords fine
and bridles and glowing wheels;

Many at the same time on the other side, in various words, an opinion
for Turnus, and the great of the queen name shelters him,
many a fame of the man supports him with earned trophies.
